  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Generally dry weather through next Saturday. \nDrought conditions will worsen.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nThe big story is dry weather persisting. Mild and dry this\n(Sunday) afternoon with temperatures 60-65 and relative \nhumidities mostly 20-30 percent.\n\nA cold front will move through from north to south during the\nday Monday and into early evening, but again, the front is\nseverely lacking deep moisture and we are looking at just a\nchance of showers, mainly in the north. Any rain totals should\nbe less than 0.10 inch, and many places will get nothing. \n\nSeasonably cool Monday night to Wednesday with high pressure\nbuilding in. Tuesday night looks quite chilly with upper teens\nto mid 20s. Afternoon relative humidities will be quite low\nTuesday/Wednesday with 30-40 percent in general.\n\nWarmer Thursday ahead of the next cold front, which moves\nthrough Thursday night into Friday. Yet again, this front does\nnot tap into any notable moisture, and we are looking at just a\nchance of rain, with any rain that does occur likely remaining\nless than 0.10 inch. \n\nDry into Halloween, but uncertainty increases as we head into\nSunday/Monday/Tuesday. Some models/ensembles bring hope of some\nwet weather, but there is substantial uncertainty and nothing we\ncan call a sure bet for rain yet.",
